WTF: MPO_EXCEPTION_PORT only where the kernel has that option

mach_port_construct's MPO_EXCEPTION_PORT is newer than Darwin 19 (Minkar's
kernel); without it the exception port is an ordinary receive right,
as it was before the option existed.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/threads/Signals.cpp	2026-11-07 01:19:27.924919030 -0500
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/threads/Signals.cpp	2026-11-07 01:19:27.956918339 -0500
@@ -131,7 +131,11 @@
     if (!handlers.addedExceptions)
         return;
 
-    uint16_t flags = MPO_INSERT_SEND_RIGHT | MPO_EXCEPTION_PORT;
+    uint16_t flags = MPO_INSERT_SEND_RIGHT;
+#if defined(MPO_EXCEPTION_PORT)
+    // A port made only for exceptions, where the kernel has that option.
+    flags |= MPO_EXCEPTION_PORT;
+#endif
 
     mach_port_options_t options { };
     options.flags = flags;
